72	    /**
73	     Determines if the input document's <b>body</b> is valid, against the safelist. It is considered valid if all the
74	     tags and attributes in the input HTML are allowed by the safelist, and that there is no content in the
75	     <code>head</code>.
76	     <p>
77	     This method is intended to be used in a user interface as a validator for user input. Note that regardless of the
78	     output of this method, the input document <b>must always</b> be normalized using a method such as
79	     {@link #clean(Document)}, and the result of that method used to store or serialize the document before later reuse
80	     such as presentation to end users. This ensures that enforced attributes are set correctly, and that any
81	     differences between how a given browser and how jsoup parses the input HTML are normalized.
82	     </p>
83	     <p>Example:
84	     <pre>{@code
85	     Document inputDoc = Jsoup.parse(inputHtml);
86	     Cleaner cleaner = new Cleaner(Safelist.relaxed());
87	     boolean isValid = cleaner.isValid(inputDoc);
88	     Document normalizedDoc = cleaner.clean(inputDoc);
89	     }</pre>
90	     </p>
91	     @param dirtyDocument document to test
92	     @return true if no tags or attributes need to be removed; false if they do
93	     */
